.TH CFIMPORT 1 "January 2026" "cfimport 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cfimport \- AWS CloudFormation Import Tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfimport
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfimport
automates the process of importing existing AWS resources into CloudFormation stacks.
It simplifies the manual steps required for CloudFormation resource imports,
including template generation, resource scanning, and stack operations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Scan AWS account for existing resources using the IaC generator.
Scans are region-wide and expire after 30 days.
.TP
.B generate
Generate CloudFormation template from scanned resources.
Creates templates with DeletionPolicy: Retain for import.
.TP
.B import
Import resources into a new or existing CloudFormation stack.
Automates change set creation and execution.
.TP
.B list
List supported resource types or resources from scans/stacks.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to configuration file (default: $HOME/.cfimport.yaml)
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output
.TP
.BR \-\-region " " \fIREGION\fR
AWS region (overrides AWS_REGION environment variable)
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " " \fIPROFILE\fR
AWS profile to use from credentials file
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show version information
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message
.SH SCAN COMMAND
.B cfimport scan
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Initiate a resource scan to discover existing AWS resources.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Output file for scan results (JSON)
.TP
.BR \-\-types " " \fITYPES\fR
Comma-separated resource types to scan for
.TP
.BR \-\-wait
Wait for scan to complete (default: true)
.SH GENERATE COMMAND
.B cfimport generate
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Generate a CloudFormation template from scanned resources.
.TP
.BR \-\-scan\-id " " \fIID\fR
Scan ID from a previous scan
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-resources " " \fIIDS\fR
Specific resource IDs to include
.TP
.BR \-\-types " " \fITYPES\fR
Resource types to include
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Output template file (default: template.yaml)
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: yaml or json (default: yaml)
.SH IMPORT COMMAND
.B cfimport import
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Import resources into a CloudFormation stack.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stack " " \fINAME\fR
Stack name (required)
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-template " " \fIFILE\fR
CloudFormation template file (required)
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-resources " " \fIFILE\fR
Resources to import JSON file (required)
.TP
.BR \-\-create
Create a new stack instead of updating existing
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Validate and create change set without executing
.TP
.BR \-\-wait
Wait for import to complete (default: true)
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan for resources in a region:
.PP
.RS
cfimport scan --region us-east-1
.RE
.PP
Generate template from scan:
.PP
.RS
cfimport generate --scan-id abc123 --output template.yaml
.RE
.PP
Import resources into existing stack:
.PP
.RS
cfimport import --stack mystack --template template.yaml --resources resources.json
.RE
.PP
Create new stack with imported resources:
.PP
.RS
cfimport import --stack newstack --template template.yaml --resources resources.json --create
.RE
.PP
Dry-run import to preview changes:
.PP
.RS
cfimport import --stack mystack --template template.yaml --resources resources.json --dry-run
.RE
.SH RESOURCES FILE FORMAT
The resources file for import should be JSON array:
.PP
.RS
[
  {
    "ResourceType": "AWS::EC2::Instance",
    "LogicalResourceId": "MyInstance",
    "ResourceIdentifier": {
      "InstanceId": "i-1234567890abcdef0"
    }
  }
]
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AWS_REGION
Default AWS region
.TP
.B AWS_PROFILE
Default AWS profile
.TP
.B AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
AWS access key ID
.TP
.B AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
AWS secret access key
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.cfimport.yaml
User configuration file
.TP
.I /etc/cfimport/config.yaml
System-wide configuration file
.TP
.I $HOME/.aws/credentials
AWS credentials file
.TP
.I $HOME/.aws/config
AWS configuration file
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error
